{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And the servant ran toward her</b> — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 24:17): because he saw that the waters rose toward her. And in Bereshit Rabbah (Genesis Rabbah 60:5), on the verse \"and she filled her pitcher and went up\" — all the other women would go down and fill from the spring, but this one, as soon as the waters saw her, immediately rose; the Holy One, blessed be He, said to her: you are a sign of blessing for your children. It appears that they inferred this from the language of \"and she filled her pitcher and went up,\" since it does not say \"and she drew and filled,\" for the miracle was performed for her on the first occasion, whereas afterward it is written \"and she drew\" (Genesis 24:20). And when the servant recounted it to them, he said (Genesis 24:45), \"and the spring came up and she drew\" — perhaps they would not have believed it."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "In the Bereshit Rabbah passage, Ramban renders the divine speaker as הקב\"ה (the Holy One, blessed be He), which I have retained per the voice rules governing divine names."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:34:04.169825390Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}